    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327">

                <pb facs="0540" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Director of War Mobilization</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Byrnes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        President</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d327-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-26">November 26, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cablegram for the President:</p>
                <p>Increased landing craft program submitted Wednesday<anchor n="2" xml:id="d327-f2"
                    /> possible only if we immediately issue directive giving priority over all
                    programs any kind. Please wire whether I shall have Nelson issue
                        directive.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d327-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d327-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d327-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the White House Map Room, via military channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d327-f2" n="2" xml:id="d327-f2-content">
                <p>November 24, 1943; <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg395">p.
                        395</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d327-f3" n="3" xml:id="d327-f3-content">
                <p>For the reply sent by Hopkins, see <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg617">p. 617</ref>. Byrnes states (<hi rendition="#italic">All In
                        One Lifetime</hi>, p. 204) that he sent another telegram to Roosevelt later
                    the same day in which he suggested that the President might count on 15 percent
                    more output than was indicated in the cautious figures in his telegram of
                    November 24, 1943. It has not been possible to find a copy of this additional
                    telegram of November 26 in official files.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
